WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.067
You look gorgeous. It is so nice
to see you in person.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.934
-I know.
It was all on Zoom last time.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.767
-We were Zooming, but
I appreciate you doing it

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:09.133
back then because we needed
to entertain people.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.200
So thank you so much.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.100
-Oh, it's so great
to be here in person.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.868
-We were talking
about "Loki"...

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.334
-Yeah.
-...before it came out.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.501
And now it's the most watched
Marvel series on Disney Plus.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:21.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I know, I know.

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.968
-It blew up, it blew up.
-I know.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.601
It just got nominated
for six Emmys.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.634
-That's right.
Well deserved. Yeah.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
How cool is that?

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.000
-Yeah, yeah.
-People love the show.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.501
What was your reaction when you
saw it become the biggest thing?

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:36.934
-Oh, it was so surreal.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.267
I mean, the whole experience
was amazing.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:44.000
And for me to join something
that has such a huge fan base.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.634
And obviously, Tom Hiddleston's

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.501
played that character
for such a long time.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:50.801
So, to be, you know,
this morally ambiguous character

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:53.567
like Ravonna Renslayer has
kind of been really cool for me.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:56.200
-It kind of introduced
the multiverse to the world.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.133
-Yeah.
-Do you understand

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.267
the multiverse?

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.767
-Does anyone understand
the multiverse?

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:01.934
-I don't know.
I'm a little -- I think I do.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.267
I act like I do.
But don't test me on it.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.701
-I know. I kind of feel
like we need a tutorial on it.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.767
When we first started
the first season of "Loki,"

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.701
Tom gave us a big "Loki"
presentation,

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.501
kind of a PowerPoint on
his character and the history.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.934
-Is that right? He explained it?

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.434
From Loki himself?
-Exactly.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.934
-That's fantastic.
-From the horse's mouth.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.667
But I feel like we need one
for the multiverse.

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.634
-Do you --
Are you filming season two?

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.567
-Yes, we just started.
-Oh, really?

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.267
-Yeah.
-Over in London, right?

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.601
-That's right, yeah.
-Everything is quiet

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:30.901
and under wraps and --

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.367
-It is. It is, I'm afraid.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.734
I'm not allowed
to give too much away, but --

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.467
But, no, it's really,
really great to be back.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.033
And it kind of
feels like, you know --

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.167
Because my character
deals with time

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.234
and the Time Variance Authority,

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.968
being back in that world,

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:45.434
it's -- it's like
no time has past.

00:01:45.434 --> 00:01:47.567
-We talked about your paintings
last time.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:51.667
You're an amazing artist.
I think you did at the time --

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.167
George Floyd was one you did.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.968
-Yeah.
-You brought a picture of one.

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.868
You did a portrait
of Kevin Hart,

00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:00.400
and it actually
looks exactly like him.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.267
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.901
-That's amazing.
Why did you --

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:10.367
Why did you choose Kevin
over...other comedians?

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.701
I'm just saying. I mean...

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.167
-No, I -- Yours is coming.
Yours is coming.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.901
-I've been with you through
some hard times, COVID.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:22.868
Zooming with you during COVID
and everything, yeah.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.501
But Kevin gets
special treatment?

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:26.868
-Yeah, well, I'll tell you
the reason I chose Kevin,

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.200
we had just finished
a movie together.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.501
We did a movie called "Lift,"
and it's set in the art world.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:36.133
It's kind of like
an action heist thriller,

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.934
and he was constantly sort of
teasing me about my painting.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.868
You know how Kevin
kind of likes to tease.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:44.567
-Of course. That's why we don't
have him back on the show.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:46.033
He's banned.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:47.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.968
-And, you know, he was
developing an interest

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:53.734
in art genuinely
during the show itself.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:54.868
-Yeah.

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.767
-And I actually, during filming,
got COVID.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:00.367
It was luckily a mild case,

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.901
but I had a bunch of time
off work.

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.267
-Right.
-Yeah, so, fortunately

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.834
it wasn't too bad,
and I got the paints out

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.534
because I was in isolation again
and so was able to give him

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.467
this painting of him as
a wrap gift.

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.467
-Did he love it?
-He loved it.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:15.300
Yeah, he was really --
It was lovely.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.501
It was really the last day of
filming and it was emotional.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.467
-I think you got his eyes
perfect because he does have

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:22.200
kind of those
little puppy-dog eyes.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.000
It almost looks like
he's crying sometimes.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.767
-I know, I know.
-"Kevin, what's wrong?"

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.267
And he's like,
"Nothing's wrong!"

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.701
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.267
-Starts yelling at me,
making fun of me, yeah.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.133
Your show, "Surface,"
let's talk about this.

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:35.100
You star and
executive produce it.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.267
-Yeah.
-That's a lot of work.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.601
-Thank you.
-Congrats on this.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.200
Can you explain --

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.634
Basically, you play a character
who's lost her memory?

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.000
-Yeah, yeah.
-And then she's trying to get

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.000
her life back together really.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.968
I play Sophie Ellis,
and the whole show

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:52.400
is a psychological thriller
set in San Francisco.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.400
And basically, at the beginning
of the show, Sophie,

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.634
we discover, has lost her memory
after an accident.

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.434
And she sort of is trying
to put the pieces

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:02.968
back of her life together.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:07.534
And she discovers that her
husband, maybe she can't trust.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.567
And the whole -- There's
so many twists and turns,

00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.267
but there's a sort of,
"did she jump

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.834
or was she pushed" element
to this accident.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.701
And we sort of
get sucked into her life

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.501
and, you know, the glamorous
world of San Francisco.

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:20.868
It's really interesting.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.767
-I want to show everyone
a clip right here.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:26.501
Here's Gugu Mbatha-Raw
in "Surface." Take a look.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:30.968
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.100
-Sir, which way
are you taking us?

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.000
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.467
♪♪

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.200
-You need to
get out of this lane.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.334
-This is the best way.
Don't worry.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:43.734
-No, no, no.
You don't understand.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:46.834
This way goes over the bridge.
I can't go over the water!

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:48.801
♪♪

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:50.868
Just -- Just pull over, please!

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.667
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:53.968
-Let me out!

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:56.434
-[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.267
[ Handle rattling ]
-What are you doing?

00:04:58.267 --> 00:05:00.767
-Let me out of the car!
-Alright!

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.300
Here. Alright. Unlocked! Go!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.067
[ Belt clicks ]

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:07.868
♪♪

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:09.968
[ Horns honking,
indistinct shouting ]

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:12.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.834
-I will say, too...

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.334
Speaking of water,

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:19.000
there's a really good
underwater scene.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.033
-Yeah.

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:21.200
-Which it's tough
to do underwater acting.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.834
-Yeah, I mean,
I've watched movies and TV shows

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.234
with underwater scenes
my whole life,

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:26.868
but I have never done one.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:30.334
And I have to say
it was kind of a real challenge.

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.834
I have to jump into this,
you know, big tank,

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:34.400
and every single time I jump --

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.968
and I just couldn't help
but sort of screw my face up.

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.801
And the director was like,
"You're screwing your face up.

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.367
You're, like, you know,
making this weird face."

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:41.801
And I'd be like,
"No, I'm not. No, I'm not.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:43.267
I'm just holding my breath,
trying to stay alive."

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:45.033
-That's what someone would do
if they go underwater.

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:46.701
-Right, right.
And he's like, "No, no.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.367
You're screwing your face up."
-"You're an actor."

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:49.567
-"Watch this.
Watch the playback."

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:51.000
And every time,
I was just like, "Mnh!"

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.267
And they were slowing it down.

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:54.667
And so it was
kind of really bad.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:56.133
But it's like --
you're in your --

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.000
You're not in your
natural element, you know,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.734
and your face does
such different things.

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.434
-So now you know how
to underwater act.

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.000
-Exactly.
-There you go.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.400
Gugu Mbatha-Raw, everybody.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:08.033
"Surface" premieres globally
July 29th on Apple TV Plus.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.834
We'll be back with standup
from Pete Lee.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.968
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

